  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": ".NET 5-11 date, globalization, and regex changes",
      "items": [
        "ICU globalization behavior became available on Windows starting in .NET 5, with ICU the default on supported systems. .NET 6 introduced DateOnly and TimeOnly; .NET 7 added source-generated regular expressions and the NonBacktracking engine; .NET 8 added TimeProvider; .NET 11 added RegexOptions.AnyNewLine. These additions affect platform consistency, testing, and regex safety but do not change the semantic difference between instants, wall-clock values, durations, and dates."
      ],
